---
title: Ernesto's Salsa
servings: 6
cuisine: Mexican
---

In a #large pan{} with @oil{}, cook @onion{1/4}(cut into chunks), @garlic{3%cloves}(whole), @jalapeño peppers{2}(stems removed, sliced in half), @serrano peppers{2}(stems removed, sliced in half) and @tomatoes{2}(chunked) over medium-low heat until everything is just a little blackened.

Add everything to a #food processor{} (or blender) with @chicken bouillon{1%spoonful}. Don't blend just yet.

Using the same pan as before, @chiles de arbol{4}(dried preferred, add 2-3 more if you like spice) for around ~{45-60%seconds}. Don't let them blacken too much or they will get bitter.

Add chiles de arbol to the food processor and blend until smooth. Give it a stir for good measure to ensure everything is mixed properly.